Enterprise IT Portfolio & Access Management System

AI Development Rules

Version: 2.0

1. General AI Coding Principles

The AI must behave as a senior enterprise software engineer.
All generated code must be:

Production-ready.

Secure.

Maintainable.

Following enterprise development standards.

Free from placeholders.

Free from TODO comments.

Never generate:

Fake implementations.

Empty methods.

Placeholder responses.

Incomplete logic.

If implementation requires multiple files, generate all required files.

2. Backend Technology Stack

Laravel 12 API

PHP 8.3+

MySQL

Laravel Sanctum

Spatie Permission

Spatie Activitylog

Maatwebsite Excel

3. PHP Coding Standards

All PHP files MUST:

Follow PSR-12 formatting.

Start with declare(strict_types=1);

All classes MUST:

Use strict typing.

Define return types and property types.

Avoid unnecessary mixed types.

Correct Example:
public function getUser(int $id): User

4. Laravel Architecture Rules

The application MUST follow a layered architecture.
Do NOT implement the Repository Pattern. Eloquent is sufficient.

Recommended structure:

app/
├── Http/
│   ├── Controllers/Api/V1/
│   ├── Requests/
│   └── Resources/
├── Services/
├── Policies/
├── Models/
└── Exceptions/


5. Controller Rules

Controllers MUST remain thin. They are responsible ONLY for:

Receiving requests.

Calling Services.

Returning Resources.

Controllers MUST NOT contain: Business logic, Database queries, Complex calculations, or Permission logic.

6. Service Layer Rules

All business logic MUST exist inside Services (app/Services).
Services handle: Business workflows, Complex operations, Transactions, and Integration logic.
Services MUST NOT: Return HTTP responses, Handle validation, or Access Request objects.

7. Validation Rules

Validation MUST exist ONLY inside Form Requests (app/Http/Requests).
Never validate inside Controllers, Services, or Models.
All validation messages must support localization using Laravel helper: __('messages.validation.required')

8. API Resource Rules

All API responses MUST use API Resources.

JsonResource (for single models)

ResourceCollection (for collections)

9. Database Rules

All database operations MUST follow:

Proper indexing on foreign keys and searchable columns.

Explicit cascade behavior or nullOnDelete().
Tables should include: id (Auto Increment, no UUIDs), created_at, updated_at, deleted_at (SoftDeletes where required).

10. Query Optimization Rules

The AI MUST prevent N+1 problems. Always use with() or loadMissing().
Enable Model strict mode in AppServiceProvider:
Model::preventLazyLoading(!app()->isProduction());

11. Database Transactions

Any multi-step write operation MUST use:
DB::transaction(function () { ... });

12. Authorization Rules

Authorization MUST use Laravel Policies mapped to Spatie Permission.
Authorization flow: Request -> Policy -> Permission -> Action.
Do not use auth()->user()->can() inside controllers. Rely on Route Middleware or $this->authorize().

13. Audit Logging Rules

All sensitive operations MUST be logged using spatie/laravel-activitylog.
Never manually insert audit records.

14. API Standards

Base API version: /api/v1

Standard Success Response:

{
    "success": true,
    "message": "Operation successful",
    "data": {},
    "errors": null
}


Validation Error Response (422):

{
    "success": false,
    "message": "Validation failed",
    "data": null,
    "errors": { "email": ["The email field is required."] }
}


15. Pagination, Search, Sorting

All index endpoints MUST support:

Pagination: ?page=1&per_page=15 (Default 15).

Search: ?search=keyword (Search indexed columns only).

Sorting: ?sort=name (ASC) or ?sort=-created_at (DESC).

16. API Security Rules

Never expose sensitive database fields. Do not trust frontend validation. Use .env for secrets.

17. Frontend Technology Stack

React 19 + Vite + TypeScript

Tailwind CSS

TailAdmin (Layout Shell)

shadcn/ui (Internal Components)

TanStack Query (React Query)

React Hook Form + Zod

React Router v7

Axios & Sonner

18. Frontend Architecture Rules

The frontend MUST follow Feature-Based Architecture. Never create flat structures.
Required structure:

src/
├── features/
│   └── featureName/
│       ├── components/
│       ├── hooks/
│       ├── services/
│       ├── pages/
│       └── types/
├── components/
├── layouts/
├── routes/
├── lib/
└── utils/


19. React Component Rules

All components MUST:

Use Functional Components with TypeScript.

Have clear responsibilities and be reusable.
Avoid: Huge components, Business logic inside JSX, and Direct API calls inside components (use hooks/services instead).

20. State Management Rules

Server State: Must use TanStack Query (API data, Cache, Pagination, Loading states).

Local UI State: Use React Hooks (Modal state, Form state, Tabs).
Do NOT introduce Redux unless explicitly required.

21. API Communication Rules

All API communication MUST go through services/.
Create a centralized Axios instance in src/lib/axios.ts to handle: Base URL, Auth tokens, Global errors, and Unauthorized handling.

22. Forms Rules

All forms MUST use React Hook Form + Zod.
Every form MUST support: Client & Backend validation errors, Loading state, Submit prevention during mutation, and Success/Error notifications (via Sonner).

23. UI Architecture Rules (Hybrid)

TailAdmin is ONLY responsible for: Layout, Sidebar, Navbar, Footer, and Dashboard shell.

shadcn/ui is used for: Buttons, Forms, Dialogs, Tables, Select, Combobox, Calendar, Alerts.
CRITICAL: When generating tailwind config, dynamically merge TailAdmin's colors and shadcn's variables. Do NOT overwrite one with the other.

24. Localization (i18n) Rules

Supported languages: Arabic (ar) / English (en).
The system MUST support:

Dynamic language switching (RTL/LTR switching).

Localized validation and API messages.

Adapt Tailwind classes using logical properties (e.g., ms- instead of ml-).

25. Date, Time and Number Formatting

Never hardcode formats. Always use localization utilities.

26. Accessibility Rules

All UI components should consider: Keyboard navigation, Proper labels, Screen reader compatibility, and Focus states.

27. Error Handling Rules

Backend: Must return structured JSON errors.

Frontend: Must handle Network errors, Validation errors, Auth expiration. Never show raw technical errors to users.

28. Loading State Rules

Every async operation MUST have: Loading indicator, Disabled submit actions. Avoid blank screens (use Skeletons).

29. Testing Requirements

Backend: Feature tests for APIs, Unit tests for Services, Authorization tests.

Frontend: Component tests, Form validation tests, Critical workflow tests.

30. Code Quality Rules

Backend: Laravel Pint, PHPStan, PHPUnit.

Frontend: ESLint, TypeScript Compiler, Prettier.
Code must pass validation before merging.

31. CI/CD Rules

Every Pull Request MUST validate:

Backend: composer install, php artisan test, vendor/bin/pint, phpstan analyse

Frontend: npm install, npm run lint, npm run type-check, npm run build

32. Environment Rules

Never hardcode URLs, Passwords, Tokens, API keys, or Database credentials. Always use .env.

33. Git Rules

Commit messages should follow Conventional Commits: type(scope): message
Examples: feat(users): add user management, fix(auth): resolve token refresh issue

34. Documentation Rules

Every feature MUST document: Feature Name, Purpose, Database Changes, API Endpoints, Permissions Required, Frontend Components.

35. AI Generation Rules

When generating code, the AI MUST:

Understand existing architecture first.

Follow current naming conventions.

Reuse existing components.

Avoid duplicated implementations.

Generate complete files with required imports.

Include migrations when database changes are required.

Include tests for critical logic.

36. Sprint Execution Rules

Each sprint implementation MUST include:

Backend: Migration, Model, Relationships, Requests, Policies, Services, Resources, Controllers, Tests.

Frontend: Types, Services, Hooks, Components, Pages, Routes, Validation.

37. Production Readiness Checklist

Before marking any feature complete, check:
[ ] Database optimized (Indexes/N+1)
[ ] Authorization & Validation implemented
[ ] API Resources used
[ ] Audit logging added
[ ] Localization completed
[ ] Tests added
[ ] No TODO comments or duplicated logic